      "official_mark_scheme_text": "$f\\prime(-1)=0$ and $f\\prime(3)=0$ give $3-a+b=0$ and $27+3a+b=0$. — M1. Guidance: stationary points at $x=-1$ and $x=3$ give simultaneous equations in $a$ and $b$.\n$a=-6$. — A1. Guidance: solve the simultaneous equations.\n$b=-9$. — A1.\nHence $f\\prime(x)=3x^2-6x-9$, so $f(x)=x^3-3x^2-9x+c$. — B1. Guidance: follow through a correct integration for their numerical $a,b$.\n$2=-1-3+9+c$. — M1. Guidance: substitute $x=-1$, $y=2$ into their integrated function; $c$ must be present.\n$c=-3$. — A1. Guidance: follow through from their function.\n$k=f(3)=27-27-27-3$. — M1. Guidance: substitute $x=3$, $y=k$ into their integrated function; allow $c$ omitted.\n$k=-30$. — A1.\nTotal: 8",
